WEBVTT

00:50.300 --> 00:51.551
When I was first hired,

00:51.634 --> 00:54.846
they had me go up
and assess prevailing visibility.

00:56.598 --> 00:59.059
I go at the same time every morning,

01:00.226 --> 01:03.229
observe my unchanging targets,
the various mountains,

01:03.313 --> 01:04.773
and calculate visibility.

01:04.856 --> 01:06.316
PREVAILING VISIBILITY

01:08.651 --> 01:11.029
MOUNT INWANG
VISIBILITY: 1.6KM

01:11.112 --> 01:12.489
BAEGUNDAE PEAK

01:12.572 --> 01:14.324
MOUNT BUGAK

01:16.701 --> 01:18.787
MOUNT BUGAK
VISIBILITY: 2.9KM

01:18.870 --> 01:20.705
I always found it strange

01:20.789 --> 01:22.373
taking my measurements every day,

01:23.416 --> 01:26.294
how much we trust human eyesight

01:27.212 --> 01:29.798
that was considered good enough to be used

01:29.881 --> 01:33.218
to assess something
as important as visibility.

01:34.844 --> 01:38.056
We usually rely on machines
for their accuracy and objectivity.

01:38.139 --> 01:41.893
Human vision can be precise,
but it's more easily distorted…

01:44.813 --> 01:46.064
narrowed…

01:48.358 --> 01:49.692
or biased…

01:56.032 --> 01:57.700
by the surrounding conditions.

03:39.677 --> 03:41.387
Get home safe last night?

03:41.471 --> 03:42.597
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

03:56.736 --> 04:01.824
EPISODE 4
VISIBILITY

04:05.328 --> 04:07.330
We're having a cool and hazy morning,

04:07.413 --> 04:09.332
with fog in several inland areas.

04:09.415 --> 04:11.876
This is likely
due to last night's temperature drop.

04:11.960 --> 04:14.629
In addition to the fog,
visibility is quite low

04:14.712 --> 04:16.256
due to fine dust in the air.

04:16.339 --> 04:18.841
We recommend being extra careful
on the road today.

04:44.033 --> 04:45.243
Sleep well?

04:49.247 --> 04:50.581
If we both feel something,

04:50.665 --> 04:52.000
we date.

04:53.001 --> 04:54.377
If not, we don't.

04:54.460 --> 04:56.129
So which is it?

04:58.214 --> 05:00.717
What are… we?

05:07.265 --> 05:08.975
We work at the same place.

05:12.979 --> 05:15.315
I'm a director and you're a forecaster.

05:15.398 --> 05:16.524
That's all we are.

05:16.607 --> 05:17.608
You don't feel more?

05:17.692 --> 05:19.652
Our feelings will fade in a while.

05:19.736 --> 05:20.737
We'll be normal again.

05:20.820 --> 05:23.323
Or regret it, someday.

05:23.406 --> 05:25.074
Well, that could be nice.

05:25.158 --> 05:27.160
Remembering the one that got away.

05:27.243 --> 05:29.287
You can't ask me to date at work again.

05:29.370 --> 05:30.580
I won't.

05:31.789 --> 05:32.999
It'd be awful.

05:33.666 --> 05:34.667
I can't.

05:37.587 --> 05:40.298
How do you feel, though, about me?

05:50.475 --> 05:53.895
I shouldn't have revealed it. Sorry.

06:02.445 --> 06:03.988
I'm not sorry at all.

06:04.697 --> 06:08.534
Why would I be sorry that you
could see I wanna be with you?

06:47.782 --> 06:50.743
Due to the thick fog,
there was a 14-car pileup

06:50.827 --> 06:54.205
on the Jungang Expressway
in Hoengseong early this morning.

06:54.831 --> 06:57.708
We announced
to expect the fog last night.

06:57.792 --> 07:00.962
And there's been news coverage about it
in current condition since 10:00 p.m.

07:01.045 --> 07:05.216
Visibility at the time of the collision
was reported as less than 100 meters.

07:05.967 --> 07:09.137
- And how precise was our forecast?
- I'd say it was at least adequate.

07:09.220 --> 07:12.056
We reported the possibility
that visibility could drop to 50 meters

07:12.140 --> 07:14.642
if the fog in Hoengseong thickened
around 2:00 a.m.,

07:14.725 --> 07:17.979
also, we sent out texts
encouraging commuters to drive cautiously.

07:18.563 --> 07:20.231
Hmm, we did what we could.

07:21.399 --> 07:23.776
How many recent accidents
have we seen in that area?

07:24.777 --> 07:27.321
Looking at the data
from the past three years,

07:27.405 --> 07:31.242
326 cases in Daegwallyeong,
Chuncheon, 115,

07:31.325 --> 07:32.952
and 109 cases in Cheorwon.

07:33.661 --> 07:36.164
Goodness, why don't they slow down
if they know fog is so common?

07:36.247 --> 07:37.206
I don't get it.

07:38.249 --> 07:40.293
Don't you think KWA's forecast approach

07:40.376 --> 07:42.462
with fog needs to change
in response to this?

07:42.545 --> 07:45.715
Well, I'll look into it and get feedback
from the other directors.

07:47.091 --> 07:49.177
Okay. Get the meeting started, then.

07:50.178 --> 07:52.346
Let us begin the morning meeting
of May 11.

07:52.430 --> 07:53.890
Let's hear from the Satellite Center.

07:53.973 --> 07:56.100
The radiative cooling has intensified

07:56.184 --> 07:58.436
- in the inland area since last night…
- Man.

07:58.519 --> 08:00.021
She knows what she's doing.

08:00.104 --> 08:01.522
And still single, right?

08:02.106 --> 08:03.816
Yeah, she was almost like Ms. Oh, though.

08:03.900 --> 08:05.151
Like who?

08:05.234 --> 08:06.944
Oh Myung-ju, the Assistant Director.

08:07.028 --> 08:09.238
Everyone thought
they'd make her director,

08:09.322 --> 08:12.074
but she married some guy here
and was always on maternity leave.

08:12.158 --> 08:14.118
They're never gonna promote her now.

08:14.202 --> 08:16.704
And how's that anything like Director Jin?

08:16.787 --> 08:18.080
You know Mr. Han?

08:18.164 --> 08:19.040
He talks to the press.

08:19.123 --> 08:21.250
You mean the guy
with thick eyebrows?

08:22.084 --> 08:25.546
They were engaged, but she broke up
with him a month before the wedding.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.798
- She dodged the bullet, then.
- Hm?

08:27.882 --> 08:29.300
She's way out of his league.

08:29.383 --> 08:32.887
You're right. It's important
for women like that

08:32.970 --> 08:34.347
to find someone who's not an idiot.

08:35.473 --> 08:38.100
Oh, how are your investments?

08:38.935 --> 08:40.728
I think it's great. I…

08:49.362 --> 08:51.822
It's time to come up
with something fresh.

08:51.906 --> 08:53.199
Team, circle around.

08:55.743 --> 08:56.744
Okay.

08:57.787 --> 08:59.455
What's the takeaway?

09:00.289 --> 09:01.541
Come on.

09:01.624 --> 09:04.502
Think about it, why do crashes
always happen in the same areas?

09:05.836 --> 09:06.796
Look.

09:06.879 --> 09:09.632
When it happened,
the visibility was ten meters.

09:09.715 --> 09:11.384
So, they could barely see
the filing cabinet.

09:11.467 --> 09:14.554
But what did we hear on the forecast?

09:15.763 --> 09:18.558
We don't do fog warnings.
And nowhere in Korea does, so…

09:18.641 --> 09:19.809
What are you saying?

09:19.892 --> 09:22.103
She's right. I wanna know
why we're so far behind. Hm?

09:22.186 --> 09:23.145
Other countries do.

09:23.729 --> 09:26.440
- I guess it's weird we don't.
- That's what I'm saying.

09:26.524 --> 09:28.776
So what I wanna know is, "Why?"

09:29.277 --> 09:31.696
Why do we keep
letting things like this happen?

09:31.779 --> 09:34.699
Maybe they're too worried
about covering their backs,

09:34.782 --> 09:36.909
petrified of forecasting wrong again.

09:37.702 --> 09:40.037
Find out what you can,
and get me a draft, okay?

09:40.121 --> 09:41.581
Use this accident,

09:41.664 --> 09:44.750
and pull some of the worst ones
from a couple of years ago. Okay?

09:44.834 --> 09:46.669
Isn't this pushing a narrative?

09:46.752 --> 09:49.338
What, don't want your husband
to look bad over at KMA?

09:49.422 --> 09:50.715
Oh! Come on, it's not that.

09:50.798 --> 09:52.967
Then take your assignment and get to work.

09:53.050 --> 09:55.636
A good journalist leaves
their personal life at home.

09:56.262 --> 09:57.471
So that's it.

09:57.555 --> 09:59.015
Good work. Good work. Back to it.

10:01.809 --> 10:04.228
- Okay. I'll get it.
- All right.

10:08.441 --> 10:10.901
Oh, did you go for a run before work?

10:10.985 --> 10:13.446
Oh, I thought I should come right away
after the crash.

10:24.749 --> 10:26.208
You got home okay last night?

10:26.292 --> 10:27.877
Yeah.

10:27.960 --> 10:31.547
So, hey, who was the lady
that snuck out the back?

10:31.631 --> 10:34.216
Who? He was with a woman?

10:35.217 --> 10:37.762
Uh, I really don't know
what you're even talking about.

10:37.845 --> 10:39.680
You do. I know what I saw.

10:39.764 --> 10:41.724
There was this woman at your table,

10:41.807 --> 10:43.726
and she snuck out
the very second we arrived.

10:43.809 --> 10:44.852
What?

10:45.478 --> 10:47.063
You have a girlfriend?

10:52.610 --> 10:54.153
No. Not right now.

10:54.236 --> 10:56.781
You're lying to us. Your poker face sucks.

10:56.864 --> 10:59.867
You can't hide someone
you really care about. You'll slip up.

11:05.748 --> 11:07.458
Well, it's not official yet.

11:07.541 --> 11:09.710
Aw, look at you.
You're dating so soon again.

11:09.794 --> 11:12.546
It's good, though.
How'd you meet? A blind date?

11:12.630 --> 11:13.756
At a club in town?

11:14.256 --> 11:17.301
No, it was through work, actually.

11:17.385 --> 11:19.387
Does she work at KMA?

11:19.470 --> 11:21.263
Do we… Just tell us her name.

11:21.347 --> 11:22.515
Did you meet at HQ?

11:22.598 --> 11:23.641
She works here?

11:24.308 --> 11:25.393
Forecaster Lee!

11:29.063 --> 11:32.108
I need a distribution chart
on the fog in Hoengseong

11:32.191 --> 11:33.859
an hour before and after the collision,

11:33.943 --> 11:35.820
and please make it
in ten-minute intervals.

11:38.114 --> 11:39.281
Maybe I should repeat myself?

11:39.365 --> 11:40.700
Oh, no, I got it all.

11:40.783 --> 11:44.203
One hour before and after the collision
in ten-minute intervals.

11:44.829 --> 11:46.455
You'll have it soon?

11:46.539 --> 11:48.499
Yeah, of course. Right away.

11:50.126 --> 11:51.544
What?

11:51.627 --> 11:53.212
She's messing with him, right?

11:53.295 --> 11:55.756
She must be. Maybe he did something?

11:58.134 --> 11:59.760
DREAM REALTY

12:02.096 --> 12:04.598
- Yes?
- Slight setback.

12:04.682 --> 12:06.976
The buyers reached out,
they went to the bank,

12:07.059 --> 12:09.645
they're backing out of the deal.

12:09.729 --> 12:10.646
Why?

12:10.730 --> 12:12.857
They had issues finalizing the bank loan.

12:13.441 --> 12:15.443
- I see.
- So, what now?

12:15.526 --> 12:18.404
Lower the price?
Going below market will sell it.

12:20.322 --> 12:21.741
So what do you think?

12:22.366 --> 12:24.493
Do it if you want to sell it quickly.

12:30.374 --> 12:33.377
Give me some time to think about it,
and then I'll call you.

13:07.036 --> 13:09.455
You know Mr. Han?
He talks to the press.

13:09.538 --> 13:13.042
They were engaged, but she broke up
with him a month before the wedding.

13:13.125 --> 13:15.252
- She dodged the bullet, then.
- Hm?

13:15.336 --> 13:16.837
She's way out of his league.

13:16.921 --> 13:19.131
You're right. It's important
for women like that

13:19.215 --> 13:21.091
to find someone who's not an idiot.

13:29.350 --> 13:31.143
What's happened to your writing?

13:31.936 --> 13:33.103
There's a problem?

13:33.187 --> 13:35.689
I know there won't be any eyes
on it outside of KMA,

13:35.773 --> 13:38.400
but still, this is sloppy.

13:38.484 --> 13:40.069
Your last column was, too.

13:40.152 --> 13:42.738
We don't need anyone saying,
"Careful not to catch a cold."

13:42.822 --> 13:45.783
Our mothers say it enough.
I want us to have more substance. Okay?

13:46.450 --> 13:47.952
You didn't mention any issues before.

13:48.536 --> 13:50.454
I thought you were just distracted.

13:50.538 --> 13:53.624
The wedding was right around the corner,
I thought it was nerves.

13:55.417 --> 13:58.087
You're not back on track yet,
so I'm getting worried.

13:58.170 --> 14:00.965
I don't know.
Fix it on the next one. Okay?

14:01.048 --> 14:02.675
You need to get it together.

14:03.425 --> 14:04.635
I didn't think it was sloppy.

14:07.096 --> 14:08.556
- Sorry, sir.
- Listen.

14:08.639 --> 14:10.307
In front of the cameras, you're great.

14:10.391 --> 14:12.935
Just give a quarter of that
to writing, okay?

14:13.018 --> 14:14.270
I'll fix it, sir.

14:15.187 --> 14:16.689
I need you alert, yeah?

14:17.273 --> 14:18.274
Yes, sir.

14:18.357 --> 14:19.692
- Yeah?
- Yes!

14:20.526 --> 14:21.861
Fix it.

14:42.256 --> 14:43.507
Did he yell at you?

14:44.049 --> 14:45.718
No, he didn't.

14:45.801 --> 14:47.469
Well, then what did he say to you?

14:47.553 --> 14:49.263
Uh, it was nothing.

14:50.890 --> 14:53.142
So, what can I do for you?

14:53.767 --> 14:57.354
Oh… The huge pileup on the expressway
in Hoengseong,

14:57.438 --> 14:59.398
it was 'cause of the fog, right?

14:59.481 --> 15:01.692
What do you mean?
The forecast was adequate.

15:01.775 --> 15:02.943
I heard that.

15:03.027 --> 15:05.654
I'd like to interview someone
about the accident.

15:05.738 --> 15:08.449
Can you get someone from the Chief Team
who will answer my questions?

15:10.242 --> 15:12.119
It's not a great time. Later, though.

15:12.202 --> 15:14.538
My deadline for the article is insane.

15:14.622 --> 15:16.624
'Cause it's due by the end of the day.

15:16.707 --> 15:18.876
Do you know how busy Chief Team is?

15:18.959 --> 15:21.921
They have more important things to do
than meet your deadlines.

15:22.004 --> 15:23.714
Well, you don't have to use that tone.

15:23.797 --> 15:25.466
You're a spokesperson.

15:25.549 --> 15:29.470
Is it so wrong to ask for a spokesperson
to coordinate an interview?

15:29.553 --> 15:31.764
- Look.
- I'm a reporter.

15:31.847 --> 15:34.600
I know. I'll try to fit it in, okay?

15:34.683 --> 15:36.226
I need to handle something first.

15:36.310 --> 15:38.354
Whatever. It's fine.

15:44.652 --> 15:45.736
Jeez.

15:46.487 --> 15:49.198
There's already way too much to do.

15:49.281 --> 15:51.742
You're making it even harder.

15:53.744 --> 15:55.120
Why?

16:19.812 --> 16:21.730
Here's the data you wanted, ma'am.

16:21.814 --> 16:24.191
I don't really understand
what you want it for, but it's completed.

16:24.274 --> 16:28.612
I'd appreciate if you'd avoid small talk
during working hours, Forecaster Lee.

16:33.575 --> 16:35.160
Thanks for this. You may go.

16:38.414 --> 16:40.040
Yes? Can I help you?

16:40.124 --> 16:42.292
Uh, no. I'm all good.

16:49.717 --> 16:52.052
He definitely did something.

16:52.136 --> 16:53.303
Definitely.

17:06.817 --> 17:07.860
Here you go.

17:11.780 --> 17:12.614
What did you do?

17:13.866 --> 17:16.785
- What?
- You did something to make her upset.

17:17.536 --> 17:19.663
Well, I made a little small talk at work.

17:20.581 --> 17:23.625
You and I both know she wouldn't
normally care about something like that.

17:24.293 --> 17:25.377
So?

17:27.171 --> 17:29.715
What are… we?

17:30.591 --> 17:31.967
We work at the same place.

17:32.051 --> 17:33.552
That's all we are.

17:34.928 --> 17:36.764
Well, she's putting up a wall.

17:37.389 --> 17:39.850
Why would she feel
like she has to do that, though?

17:39.933 --> 17:42.561
"Just 'cause I'm young
doesn't mean I'm less of a director.

17:42.644 --> 17:45.272
Cut the attitude right now
and fall in line, rookie."

17:46.065 --> 17:47.149
Could that be a clue?

17:47.232 --> 17:48.817
You were rude to her?

17:48.901 --> 17:50.235
Oh!

17:52.738 --> 17:55.407
I told you HQ is too strict for you.

17:55.491 --> 17:57.868
Huh? It's not like the Metro Office.

17:57.951 --> 17:59.578
Oh, man.

18:01.121 --> 18:03.040
It's worse
that it's Director Jin Ha-kyung.

18:03.123 --> 18:06.043
I never met
such a detail-oriented perfectionist.

18:06.668 --> 18:10.255
You know, she's more conservative
than I expected her to be.

18:10.339 --> 18:12.466
She's not like you,
going with the flow, here and there.

18:12.549 --> 18:14.009
It'll probably get worse.

18:14.551 --> 18:15.928
And so it is.

18:18.180 --> 18:19.765
Anyway, find a place?

18:19.848 --> 18:20.808
Not yet.

18:21.308 --> 18:24.436
'Cause everything is out of my budget,
or they're way too small and run-down.

18:25.604 --> 18:27.606
Do you have any leads?

18:27.689 --> 18:28.690
Oh, no, I don't.

18:28.774 --> 18:30.943
I just thought that you needed a reminder.

18:31.026 --> 18:34.113
Oh, and uh, try to be good
and listen to Director Jin.

18:34.196 --> 18:36.490
Don't put too much into dating right now.

18:36.573 --> 18:37.741
You don't have time.

18:47.376 --> 18:49.962
The surface temperature
will drop again tomorrow morning

18:50.045 --> 18:52.339
from radiative cooling, correct?

18:52.422 --> 18:56.093
Oh, yeah. There'll be a big difference
between day and night temperatures.

18:56.802 --> 19:00.889
Since it's gonna be similar,
we can use yesterday's follow-up report--

19:00.973 --> 19:03.142
Maybe we should extend the range?

19:03.225 --> 19:04.977
That would be
too wide to be useful.

19:05.811 --> 19:07.437
What if we break down each area?

19:07.521 --> 19:13.110
And we can emphasize the valleys,
streams, and any other unique areas.

19:15.320 --> 19:18.907
So we know that the fog
is the worst between 3:00 and 7:00 a.m.

19:18.991 --> 19:22.661
And in that window, most people
are on the expressway, not roads.

19:25.622 --> 19:27.040
You're getting too close.

19:27.124 --> 19:30.502
It doesn't solve how different conditions
are within the region.

19:30.586 --> 19:33.088
Look at route over three,
it gets a lot of sun.

19:33.172 --> 19:35.841
We can expect that fog
to clear up by sunrise.

19:37.134 --> 19:39.011
Too close. And it bothers you?

19:42.097 --> 19:46.185
According to the observational data
you recorded yesterday,

19:46.268 --> 19:47.436
you saw high humidity?

19:48.020 --> 19:49.980
I know that region really well.

19:50.063 --> 19:53.317
Everyone expects the fog
to be very intense this time of year.

19:54.610 --> 19:56.528
You sure are an expert in everything.

19:57.112 --> 19:59.114
You knew all about the climate
in the West Sea

19:59.198 --> 20:00.574
from being onboard the weather ship,

20:00.657 --> 20:03.535
and you're well-versed in the fog patterns
in Gangwon Province, too?

20:03.619 --> 20:05.996
I was on that weather ship
and I happened to work in Gangwon.

20:06.079 --> 20:09.458
And I'm confident that I know the terrain
of those areas like the back of my hand.

20:09.541 --> 20:11.418
And I'm accounting for the climate change.

20:11.501 --> 20:14.254
I consider all my life experiences
to be like live data.

20:14.338 --> 20:16.548
You've only seen them through computers,
I am the expert.

20:17.299 --> 20:19.885
- Then what do you recommend?
- It's up to you.

20:19.968 --> 20:21.637
You could break it down by area, though.

20:27.935 --> 20:28.977
I say…

20:29.686 --> 20:31.188
We give a regional warning.

20:31.271 --> 20:34.650
No, we have to separate it into areas,
and give warnings to each one.

20:34.733 --> 20:36.443
At least for every bridge and tunnel.

20:36.526 --> 20:39.071
- It's not up to you.
- When you all doubted the hail

20:39.154 --> 20:40.405
and that it will rain,

20:41.323 --> 20:42.449
I knew it was coming.

20:47.663 --> 20:51.375
Oh, given the time of year
and how often there are accidents

20:51.458 --> 20:55.170
all along the expressway,
a regional warning would be enough.

20:55.254 --> 20:56.255
Did you hear that?

20:56.338 --> 21:01.093
I see how a breakdown by area
could be useful if we give details.

21:01.176 --> 21:04.346
- He gets it.
- Regardless, because we know

21:04.429 --> 21:08.350
that Gangwon is almost guaranteed
to be foggy tomorrow morning,

21:08.433 --> 21:11.270
we can start working
on a preliminary report, right?

21:11.353 --> 21:12.562
That way, we're not waiting on you.

21:12.646 --> 21:15.148
- I think we need… Well…
- Without a full plan?

21:15.732 --> 21:18.110
Of course, we can touch base
throughout the day.

21:18.777 --> 21:21.863
And if we can agree on a plan,
then it turns to the night team's concern.

21:22.364 --> 21:24.074
We're late. We have to get a report done.

21:26.159 --> 21:26.994
Right?

21:30.038 --> 21:30.998
Right?

21:31.665 --> 21:32.791
I'm calling from HQ.

21:32.874 --> 21:34.835
Uh, we sent over some information
about the fog.

21:34.918 --> 21:36.128
Did it go through?

21:36.712 --> 21:37.921
Oh, good.

21:38.005 --> 21:41.675
Please send out a fog warning
for tomorrow morning to the entire region.

21:41.758 --> 21:43.343
As for breakdowns by area?

21:48.640 --> 21:51.518
I'll write them out myself,
and I'll call back with some updates.

21:51.601 --> 21:52.644
Thanks.

22:04.281 --> 22:07.075
CUSTOMER SURPRISE SERVICE INDEX
CATEGORY: MATCHMAKING SERVICE

22:07.159 --> 22:09.995
SEOUL AWARD CERTIFICATE
NUBO, MATCHMAKING SERVICE

22:11.496 --> 22:14.458
You said your daughter
is, um, a Class Five civil servant?

22:14.541 --> 22:16.251
Ah, yes.

22:16.335 --> 22:19.046
And she didn't just wait to level up.

22:19.129 --> 22:21.048
They chose her
from a pool of recruits,

22:21.131 --> 22:23.383
since her test scores
were second best of anyone there.

22:23.467 --> 22:24.551
Wow.

22:24.634 --> 22:27.637
Ma, let's go home. We can leave.

22:27.721 --> 22:28.805
Don't say anything.

22:28.889 --> 22:30.807
Ha-kyung's never gonna speak to you again.

22:30.891 --> 22:32.809
If you're so scared, then you should go.

22:32.893 --> 22:33.977
All right.

22:34.061 --> 22:35.479
Oh, did she do well?

22:35.562 --> 22:38.357
One minute.
Based on her algorithm, she is…

22:38.440 --> 22:41.735
Come on, it's Ha-kyung.
I'm sure she's ranked very high.

22:41.818 --> 22:44.154
She's like galbi beef, the best.

22:44.237 --> 22:46.907
Ma, don't say she's like beef.
That's so weird.

22:46.990 --> 22:48.533
Ha-kyung's not a piece of meat.

22:49.117 --> 22:51.078
Will you stop?

22:53.246 --> 22:55.040
- She places at Level Eight.
- What?

22:55.791 --> 22:57.042
How is she Level Eight?

22:57.125 --> 23:00.545
No, please don't worry.
Level Eight is quite respectable.

23:04.341 --> 23:07.969
You said my Ha-kyung is only Level Eight?
I don't understand.

23:08.053 --> 23:10.680
She scored in the top percentile
of every test she's taken

23:10.764 --> 23:11.807
since she was a kid.

23:11.890 --> 23:13.600
Well, this is no standard test.

23:13.683 --> 23:16.436
We say marriage
is one family joining the other.

23:16.520 --> 23:19.272
And because of that,
we look beyond a person's job.

23:19.356 --> 23:21.525
Personal information plays a big role.

23:21.608 --> 23:24.486
But so do the parents and siblings,

23:24.569 --> 23:27.656
everything is taken into account
to determine the ranking.

23:27.739 --> 23:28.949
So you…

23:29.741 --> 23:32.494
lowered her score,
because I'm a single mother?

23:32.577 --> 23:35.122
No, that's not what I said. It's not that.

23:35.622 --> 23:37.707
Obviously, you did
a great job raising her.

23:37.791 --> 23:39.251
The bigger issue is your income.

23:39.334 --> 23:41.962
It's almost impossible
to raise two kids on your own,

23:42.045 --> 23:44.256
then you expect me to get rich
while doing it?

23:44.840 --> 23:46.091
Ridiculous.

23:46.174 --> 23:48.218
See, Ma? I told you it's a waste of time.

23:49.010 --> 23:50.178
I should clarify,

23:50.262 --> 23:52.889
parents need more than 20 billion won
to make the top level.

23:55.100 --> 23:58.854
Honestly, there are a lot of doctors,
even lawyers that only rank Level Seven.

23:58.937 --> 24:03.400
Even doctors and lawyers
can rank as low as Level Seven?

24:03.483 --> 24:05.652
That's what I'm trying to tell you, ma'am.

24:05.735 --> 24:06.945
Level Eight is full of

24:07.028 --> 24:09.865
all sorts of public servants,
even public officials.

24:09.948 --> 24:11.783
There's no reason to be worried at all.

24:11.867 --> 24:13.452
I guarantee we'll find someone

24:13.535 --> 24:16.455
that is at least an equal
for your daughter.

24:16.538 --> 24:17.622
Come on.

24:21.126 --> 24:22.419
Hmm…

24:31.303 --> 24:32.512
Now is a fun part.

24:32.596 --> 24:35.307
We get to make the plan
of how we'll get her to her wedding day.

24:35.390 --> 24:36.475
Are you ready?

24:40.145 --> 24:42.814
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

24:44.608 --> 24:46.359
You've been busy all day.

24:46.443 --> 24:50.030
Yeah, I have this high-priority article,
and I've got to get an interview.

24:53.408 --> 24:55.577
What? What did you wanna say?

24:55.660 --> 24:59.122
It's the forecaster from before,
Lee Si-woo, right?

25:00.499 --> 25:02.042
Yeah, I really don't know the guy.

25:02.125 --> 25:04.836
Well, I heard a rumor
he broke up with his girlfriend.

25:06.296 --> 25:07.380
So?

25:08.423 --> 25:10.050
Introduce us.

25:12.260 --> 25:14.429
You have so many other options,
it seems risky.

25:14.513 --> 25:17.307
I don't know why you'd wanna date
a co-worker, anyway.

25:17.390 --> 25:18.808
People will be all in your business.

25:18.892 --> 25:20.560
It wouldn't be that bad.

25:21.228 --> 25:24.814
Work's so boring. We sit and write
and don't talk to anyone.

25:25.357 --> 25:27.984
I mean, it worked for you. Please?

25:28.068 --> 25:28.944
We'll see.

25:29.027 --> 25:31.112
We're not really that close.
I don't know him.

25:31.196 --> 25:32.322
You're better off on your own.

25:34.824 --> 25:36.493
Chae Yu-jin. Hey.

25:36.576 --> 25:38.828
Ugh, come on.

25:52.425 --> 25:55.387
I can't believe how popular Mr. Lee is
with the girls, you know?

25:56.221 --> 25:57.222
It's silly.

25:57.305 --> 26:00.433
It really makes me wonder.
Who could he be dating from the office?

26:01.101 --> 26:03.270
I think it's best to just ignore it all.

26:06.106 --> 26:08.400
I wish I could. I just need to know
since she's here.

26:09.234 --> 26:10.277
Oh, she's here?

26:10.360 --> 26:12.279
Well, he said they met at work.

26:12.362 --> 26:16.074
It could be someone from the Metro Office,
then she might not be here at all.

26:16.157 --> 26:17.951
I saw her, so she must be here.

26:18.034 --> 26:21.204
We showed up, and she started crawling
through the back door.

26:21.288 --> 26:23.665
If she's not here,
why would she try and hide?

26:23.748 --> 26:26.001
I heard him say they're not official.

26:26.084 --> 26:28.378
At least I thought I did, earlier.

26:28.461 --> 26:30.338
And so I take it that you heard it all.

26:30.422 --> 26:34.009
Accidentally, if you're in the same room,
you hear things.

26:34.593 --> 26:36.845
I just hope you're not
being too hard on him.

26:36.928 --> 26:38.597
He's just new. Don't hate him.

26:39.222 --> 26:40.599
I don't hate anyone.

26:42.601 --> 26:45.312
All right, I'll keep you updated.
I'm gonna find her.

26:46.646 --> 26:48.356
It's just a matter of time now.

26:55.113 --> 26:56.323
Ugh.

26:56.406 --> 26:58.617
Office romance
will be the death of me.

26:59.743 --> 27:01.036
THE ATMOSPHERE

27:01.119 --> 27:02.871
Okay, should we get out of here?

27:04.706 --> 27:06.291
- See you tomorrow.
- Goodbye.

27:06.374 --> 27:07.626
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

27:09.169 --> 27:10.712
Ah… Uh-oh.

27:11.212 --> 27:14.007
The night team should take over all that.

27:14.090 --> 27:17.719
Why waste all your time writing out
the fog breakdown yourself?

27:17.802 --> 27:20.930
I made a promise to the Gangwon Office
that I'd send it by midnight.

27:21.014 --> 27:23.725
Ugh, I said to watch your attitude,
not be teacher's pet.

27:23.808 --> 27:26.311
Well, actually, I thought
this might help her like me more.

27:26.394 --> 27:27.479
Jeez.

27:27.562 --> 27:29.564
- Don't pull an all-nighter, okay?
- Okay.

27:29.648 --> 27:30.899
- See you.
- Good luck.

27:43.870 --> 27:45.246
Got it under control?

27:46.247 --> 27:47.707
Yup. I'm good. Thanks.

27:48.625 --> 27:50.210
Okay. Goodbye, then.

27:50.293 --> 27:51.294
Bye.

27:53.505 --> 27:54.923
Turn around.

27:55.006 --> 27:57.050
Turn around.

27:57.842 --> 27:59.052
Turn around.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.222
She didn't do it.

28:14.401 --> 28:15.985
Doors opening.

28:28.289 --> 28:29.666
Doors closing.

28:49.853 --> 28:51.020
Excuse me.

28:52.856 --> 28:54.399
Would you do an interview?

28:55.483 --> 28:56.693
An interview for what?

28:58.319 --> 28:59.946
It's for an article I'm writing.

29:00.029 --> 29:01.906
I need an opinion from a director.

29:02.574 --> 29:04.826
I understand if it's too uncomfortable.

29:14.794 --> 29:18.715
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

29:20.341 --> 29:21.926
You have writer's block?

29:24.053 --> 29:25.138
Mm-hm.

29:29.601 --> 29:31.352
What's this? In May?

29:31.436 --> 29:33.104
- That's the front?
- Mm.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.314
Hm…

29:36.900 --> 29:38.193
May…

29:39.402 --> 29:42.864
In May, the weather is nice,
so people go outside more.

29:42.947 --> 29:43.823
Mm-hm.

29:44.908 --> 29:48.328
You could do some tips
on how to plan using our forecast.

29:48.411 --> 29:49.746
- You think?
- Mm-hm.

29:50.663 --> 29:52.540
And then for the title…

29:52.624 --> 29:57.587
You could do,
"Reading Forecast Like Professionals."

29:57.670 --> 29:58.922
- It's good.
- It's too wordy.

29:59.005 --> 30:00.089
- I think it's great.
- Really?

30:00.173 --> 30:01.007
- Yeah.
- Okay.

30:01.090 --> 30:03.176
- "Reading… Forecast…"
- "Forecast."

30:03.259 --> 30:06.095
- "Like the Professional…"
- "Like Professionals."

30:06.179 --> 30:08.640
Then you just say what you do,
how they can get

30:08.723 --> 30:10.558
the most out of the forecast.

30:35.917 --> 30:38.378
So, there have been lots
of accidents from the fog lately.

30:39.003 --> 30:41.089
There isn't anything very special
about the recent fog.

30:41.172 --> 30:42.966
The DTR is predictably high

30:43.049 --> 30:46.052
in February, April, and May,
August, and October,

30:46.135 --> 30:49.556
so expect a certain amount of fog
in those months.

30:49.639 --> 30:52.350
Accidents predictably go up,
then, as well.

30:52.433 --> 30:54.269
Regionally, though, there have been a lot

30:54.352 --> 30:57.605
of fog-related accidents
in Gangwon, specifically.

30:57.689 --> 31:01.109
If you check the Seohae Bridge,
it likely has many accidents.

31:02.360 --> 31:06.364
So then, why is our country behind
on implementing fog advisories?

31:08.032 --> 31:08.992
Um…

31:09.075 --> 31:10.577
It would be difficult to do them here,

31:10.660 --> 31:12.787
because of the geography
around the country.

31:12.871 --> 31:14.914
Accurate fog advisories would take

31:14.998 --> 31:18.293
a different type of equipment
for monitoring moisture particles.

31:18.376 --> 31:20.044
We need them set up every two kilometers.

31:20.128 --> 31:23.673
And it'd be impossible to do
on the budget allotted for KMA.

31:23.756 --> 31:26.801
So it's an issue of not
having enough money or equipment?

31:26.885 --> 31:28.303
And there's nothing we can do?

31:31.681 --> 31:33.808
Is there an angle you're trying to push?

31:34.434 --> 31:36.185
The only angle I'm looking for
is the truth.

31:38.646 --> 31:42.984
It's true that the recent collision
on the expressway happened

31:43.067 --> 31:45.612
because the visibility
was quite low from the fog.

31:46.404 --> 31:49.532
But we did forecast the fog,
we just couldn't say exact visibility.

31:50.116 --> 31:52.702
- Is that true enough for you?
- I think that's up to the public.

31:52.785 --> 31:54.078
They have the final say here.

32:04.380 --> 32:05.924
Things okay at your house?

32:06.007 --> 32:07.467
Man, I…

32:08.509 --> 32:10.678
- Everything's all right.
- Really?

32:12.430 --> 32:15.058
It could be awkward, and then it won't be.

32:16.017 --> 32:17.226
Hey.

32:17.310 --> 32:18.895
Was it like that for you?

32:20.855 --> 32:22.440
You know where I stand.

32:22.523 --> 32:25.610
I always hated being away from my family
and I'd fight it when I could.

32:25.693 --> 32:28.446
And if I couldn't, I bring them
to wherever I was dispatched.

32:28.529 --> 32:31.115
- Hm.
- It was only two years

32:31.199 --> 32:34.452
that we were fully separated,
when my kid was getting ready for college.

32:34.535 --> 32:35.787
Ah.

32:35.870 --> 32:37.997
When my term was finally over,

32:38.706 --> 32:41.417
it took a long time
before things were normal again.

32:41.501 --> 32:43.920
So? So, I've gotta wait it out.

32:44.504 --> 32:46.756
I… That's not what I said at all.

32:46.839 --> 32:49.092
You can't just wait.
You have to take initiative.

32:49.175 --> 32:50.760
You have to push. Okay?

32:50.843 --> 32:53.721
If you keep withdrawing
because it's hard and awkward,

32:53.805 --> 32:56.307
you're just gonna stay an outsider
in your own family.

32:56.391 --> 32:57.392
Get it?

32:58.977 --> 33:00.979
At least, that's how it felt for us.

33:01.062 --> 33:02.563
It's food for thought.

33:02.647 --> 33:04.023
Right.

33:05.984 --> 33:10.113
How long do you think
until I feel like it's home again?

33:10.196 --> 33:11.406
Does that come back?

33:11.489 --> 33:13.241
Months, tops? A year?

33:13.324 --> 33:15.535
It depends on if you push.

33:16.411 --> 33:17.578
Makes sense.

33:36.264 --> 33:37.473
Hey.

33:45.064 --> 33:47.191
Watching something funny?

33:49.610 --> 33:51.446
Show me.

33:52.113 --> 33:54.449
You can't just look at my phone.

33:55.366 --> 33:56.784
I didn't see anything.

33:59.787 --> 34:01.998
We're family. So what if I did?

34:26.564 --> 34:29.233
Do you need my help with anything?

34:29.317 --> 34:30.401
I'm set.

34:31.027 --> 34:32.528
Here. I'll get it. Let me…

34:32.612 --> 34:33.738
Wait!

34:33.821 --> 34:35.406
- Ooh!
- Ahh!

34:37.033 --> 34:38.576
- Oh, shoot.
- Oh, no.

34:38.659 --> 34:40.703
You've gotta be kidding me, Dong-han.

34:40.787 --> 34:42.997
Why couldn't you just listen?

34:43.081 --> 34:45.625
Instead of rushing in and making a mess?

34:45.708 --> 34:48.127
I thought I should help my wife.

34:48.211 --> 34:50.713
You can't help if you don't know
what you're doing.

34:50.797 --> 34:52.673
You have no idea how we do things.

34:55.176 --> 34:58.721
Don't you think that you…
you're being really harsh about things?

34:59.889 --> 35:02.892
Whatever. I'm sorry we had
to live apart for 14 years.

35:03.893 --> 35:05.603
I had no choice. I had to go.

35:06.729 --> 35:09.649
What, you think I wanted
to leave you, huh?

35:09.732 --> 35:13.528
You know there was no way.
It was too expensive to move everyone.

35:14.278 --> 35:16.739
I have always been faithful to you,
you know?

35:17.365 --> 35:19.325
My first priority is providing for you.

35:19.408 --> 35:23.955
So it'd mean a lot if you could just say,
"We missed you. Thanks for your work."

35:24.038 --> 35:26.499
It's been 14 years,
and you can't say that once?

35:27.083 --> 35:29.377
I see people more excited
about a dog coming home.

35:29.460 --> 35:31.879
Are you… Are you gonna punish me forever?

35:35.383 --> 35:37.135
- Is that all?
- No.

35:38.136 --> 35:40.138
You think that sending money every month

35:40.221 --> 35:43.558
and not cheating even once
was all we needed from you?

35:44.142 --> 35:47.103
What else? More?
What more could you need from me?

35:48.062 --> 35:50.398
Do you remember when Bo-mi was born?

35:52.441 --> 35:53.734
Yeah, she was…

35:53.818 --> 35:55.194
I was on…

35:55.278 --> 35:57.530
You were on a weather ship
out in the South Sea.

35:58.114 --> 35:59.949
You didn't even meet her
for the first time

36:00.032 --> 36:01.492
until she was three months old.

36:01.576 --> 36:04.328
Right. There was nothing I could do.

36:04.412 --> 36:06.747
What happened on her first day of school?

36:07.915 --> 36:09.792
First day of school, I was…

36:09.876 --> 36:13.296
On Baengnyeong Island,
you sent her one text.

36:14.046 --> 36:16.632
I know. We already went over that one.

36:16.716 --> 36:18.634
The way things were back then,

36:18.718 --> 36:20.928
there wasn't any time for me to get away.

36:21.012 --> 36:22.889
Right. Nothing you could do, again.

36:24.974 --> 36:26.058
Oh, and you should know.

36:27.351 --> 36:31.647
Everyone in this neighborhood thought
I was raising her on my own.

36:31.731 --> 36:32.857
They what?

36:33.608 --> 36:35.276
Who said? Tell me who said that.

36:37.278 --> 36:38.946
The whole neighborhood.

36:40.156 --> 36:41.657
When Bo-mi got sick,

36:41.741 --> 36:45.036
I strapped her to my back
and carried her to the hospital.

36:45.870 --> 36:48.414
If I brought her
to the grocery store with me,

36:48.497 --> 36:49.498
we'd get free food,

36:49.582 --> 36:52.418
'cause even the bag boy thought
I was a single mom.

36:54.378 --> 36:56.547
I had to figure out how to tell the truth.

36:57.673 --> 36:59.300
All you care about is weather.

36:59.383 --> 37:02.845
Any kind of weather,
you'll go sun, you'll go storm, you'll go.

37:02.929 --> 37:06.474
You'll wander around the whole world,
and maybe stop at home for a day.

37:06.557 --> 37:09.143
Then the next morning, you'd tell me
you would have to leave again

37:09.227 --> 37:10.436
for some stupid reason, right?

37:10.519 --> 37:12.313
You were never there. Ever.

37:15.191 --> 37:17.068
So we've tried to move on.

37:18.027 --> 37:20.446
We've made it 14 years without you.

37:21.739 --> 37:23.574
You understand me now?

38:15.960 --> 38:19.171
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

38:41.736 --> 38:42.737
MESSAGE FROM SPACE

38:42.820 --> 38:44.322
AN INTRODUCTION
TO DYNAMIC METEOROLOGY

38:44.405 --> 38:47.199
THE ENCYCLOPEDIA
OF WEATHER AND CLIMATE CHANGE

38:58.711 --> 39:00.171
THOSE WHO FIGHT WEATHER

39:00.254 --> 39:03.382
"Those Who Fight Weather. By Chae Yu-jin."

39:10.222 --> 39:11.849
Ah, cute.

39:25.154 --> 39:26.989
Hey, is everything okay?

39:27.698 --> 39:30.409
Wasn't he that psycho
that tried to wreck the wedding?

39:30.493 --> 39:33.621
Who? That guy?
No, there's absolutely no way.

39:34.622 --> 39:35.748
Are you sure?

39:35.831 --> 39:38.084
Wouldn't that be wild?

39:57.728 --> 40:00.189
WHY DOESN'T KOREA…

40:17.998 --> 40:19.917
Oh, my god.

40:23.295 --> 40:25.923
- Is she really gonna kill me?
- No.

40:28.426 --> 40:30.719
Maybe I should have asked her
before signing her up.

40:30.803 --> 40:32.179
Wow.

40:33.139 --> 40:36.559
Did you hear any of what I was saying
before we met with that lady?

40:36.642 --> 40:37.810
See, I told you.

40:37.893 --> 40:39.520
Of course, we should have asked her first.

40:40.479 --> 40:41.939
I did it, because it's best for her.

40:42.022 --> 40:43.607
More like it's best for you.

40:43.691 --> 40:45.734
You're embarrassed to tell people
that they called off the wedding

40:45.818 --> 40:48.654
so you're trying to marry her off fast
to the first decent guy you find.

40:48.737 --> 40:50.739
You have no idea.

41:05.087 --> 41:06.422
Get home safe?

41:10.301 --> 41:12.219
Yeah. H-A-U?

41:13.929 --> 41:15.055
No, no, no.

41:15.139 --> 41:17.349
Keep it professional, text formally.

41:19.101 --> 41:20.686
Forecaster Lee.

41:21.437 --> 41:23.564
Thank you for your hard work today.

41:24.064 --> 41:25.441
Are you still at…

41:27.610 --> 41:29.153
No way.

41:30.404 --> 41:32.031
Not today.

41:39.747 --> 41:40.623
LEE SI-WOO

42:07.358 --> 42:09.235
He seriously loves the sky.

42:17.535 --> 42:18.577
Oh!

42:18.661 --> 42:20.788
- No, no. Hang up!
- Director Jin?

42:20.871 --> 42:23.082
Oh, Forecaster. How's work?

42:23.165 --> 42:25.626
Good. I'm almost done for the night.

42:25.709 --> 42:27.419
Is there something you wanted?

42:27.503 --> 42:30.881
Oh, I wanted to check in
and make sure everything is all right.

42:30.965 --> 42:34.385
Hey, I bet you thought I'd leave early
and I wouldn't get it done, didn't you?

42:34.468 --> 42:36.011
No, I have faith in you.

42:36.637 --> 42:39.098
Then it must be,
you wanted to see my face?

42:40.516 --> 42:41.600
Definitely not.

42:41.684 --> 42:44.103
Why did you call, then?
It's terribly late.

42:44.186 --> 42:48.440
Uh, well, I… You need to find cases
from other countries

42:48.524 --> 42:50.943
that have fogs like we do,
and I need them in the morning.

42:51.610 --> 42:53.195
- Huh?
- And look into what countries

42:53.279 --> 42:55.447
have local fog advisories,

42:55.531 --> 42:58.367
and what equipment and methods
they use, and their budgets.

42:58.450 --> 42:59.493
Budget's important.

43:00.327 --> 43:01.745
You… You need it tomorrow?

43:02.913 --> 43:04.164
Does this seem like a joke?

43:05.291 --> 43:07.042
Uh, no, ma'am.

43:07.835 --> 43:10.754
Okay. I'm gonna expect this on my desk.

43:10.838 --> 43:12.840
- That's all.
- Okay.

43:16.844 --> 43:18.804
Okay. Great cover.

43:20.264 --> 43:21.515
What?

43:22.433 --> 43:24.226
Why is her wall have to be so high?

43:34.486 --> 43:35.613
Hello.

43:38.574 --> 43:40.951
- Hey.
- Oh, good morning.

43:42.036 --> 43:43.287
What's all this?

43:43.370 --> 43:47.082
Oh, Director Jin told me to look up
countries that have fog problems

43:47.166 --> 43:49.251
and the countries
that have local fog advisories.

43:51.378 --> 43:53.464
Wait, were you here all night?

43:53.547 --> 43:55.633
It's nothing new, honestly.

43:55.716 --> 43:57.635
We did it in training.

43:57.718 --> 44:01.221
Oh, no, your little smile,
it's breaking my heart.

44:01.305 --> 44:04.183
The bags under your eyes
are gonna hang down to your chin.

44:04.266 --> 44:06.852
It's okay. It was important.
Director Jin said it was urgent.

44:07.728 --> 44:09.188
Is it really urgent, though?

44:10.105 --> 44:11.690
It's not just busywork?

44:11.774 --> 44:12.733
What?

44:14.068 --> 44:16.654
- You guys think she did it?
- Yeah.

44:17.738 --> 44:19.990
- Did what?
- There's this…

44:20.074 --> 44:24.036
this thing that the superiors do
to put people in line.

44:24.995 --> 44:27.122
I'm sorry to tell you, it's a prank.

44:29.792 --> 44:32.127
Hey, she wouldn't. Hey!

44:35.214 --> 44:37.174
- Good morning, everyone.
- Morning.

44:43.430 --> 44:47.393
- What's the deal? Something happened?
- No, ma'am. But I think he has a report.

44:50.062 --> 44:52.523
- Here.
- Hm? What's all this?

44:52.606 --> 44:55.776
It's the report you asked for
when you called last night.

44:56.944 --> 44:59.822
You really needed it today, right?

45:00.572 --> 45:04.827
- I stayed up all night for you.
- I certainly did. Thank you.

45:04.910 --> 45:07.705
Director Jin, you should see this.

45:07.788 --> 45:08.956
What is it?

45:23.679 --> 45:25.764
- The hell is this, Han?
- Hm?

45:25.848 --> 45:27.975
You're gonna pretend you didn't know that?

45:29.309 --> 45:30.644
WHY DOESN'T KOREA
HAVE FOG ADVISORIES?

45:30.728 --> 45:33.188
INCOMPETENT KMA BLAMES IT
ON TIGHT BUDGET!

45:35.482 --> 45:36.817
REPORTER CHAE YU-JIN

45:38.902 --> 45:40.654
You had no idea this was happening?

45:48.203 --> 45:50.497
I'm sorry, sir. I wasn't aware.

45:50.581 --> 45:54.668
Seriously? It's by your wife.
You should know. How did this happen?

46:27.951 --> 46:30.078
- What is this?
- An article.

46:31.330 --> 46:34.625
The quotes you credited as mine
were not what I told you yesterday.

46:34.708 --> 46:37.252
Reporters should have enough integrity
not to twist facts.

46:37.836 --> 46:39.546
Exactly which part was twisted?

46:39.630 --> 46:40.506
Everything.

46:40.589 --> 46:43.175
I told you why we can't do advisories,
we have no choice.

46:43.258 --> 46:44.760
And that's what the article says.

46:44.843 --> 46:46.178
What's the issue, then?

46:48.013 --> 46:51.141
You must not have understood what I said.
Korea's geography.

46:51.225 --> 46:53.852
The Taebaek and the Hamgyong Mountains
lean toward the east,

46:53.936 --> 46:55.604
and the eastern-facing side
is particularly steep

46:55.687 --> 46:57.147
while the west is totally flat.

46:57.231 --> 47:00.150
The Seoul valley to Wonsan
is long and narrow.

47:00.234 --> 47:02.694
It's the same shape
as the Chugaryeong Tectonic Valley.

47:02.778 --> 47:03.904
Yeah, and?

47:03.987 --> 47:04.863
What about it?

47:06.949 --> 47:08.784
I'll say it another way for you.

47:08.867 --> 47:11.119
Meteorologists from around the world say

47:11.203 --> 47:13.080
the country with some
of the most fickle weather,

47:13.163 --> 47:15.707
the toughest in the world
to forecast is here,

47:15.791 --> 47:17.167
the Republic of Korea.

47:17.251 --> 47:19.419
It's a peninsula where 70 percent
of the land is mountainous.

47:19.503 --> 47:22.047
We have 11 major rivers
and over 1,000 dams.

47:22.130 --> 47:24.883
Regardless of terrain,
fogs are very localized.

47:24.967 --> 47:26.885
For those reasons,
we can't do local advisories,

47:26.969 --> 47:27.970
it's ineffective.

47:28.053 --> 47:31.431
The only way you'd think we're incompetent
is that you had misunderstood.

47:33.183 --> 47:34.393
Please.

47:34.893 --> 47:37.437
You explicitly said it requires equipment
we just don't have,

47:37.521 --> 47:39.648
and getting the equipment
is outside our budget.

47:39.731 --> 47:42.776
Which is the excuse that
every government department uses

47:42.860 --> 47:44.361
as cover-up.

47:45.362 --> 47:47.781
- An excuse?
- That's what it is.

47:47.865 --> 47:50.200
Your yearly budget
is over 400 billion won.

47:50.284 --> 47:52.035
If you have that much money,

47:52.119 --> 47:54.663
you can't say that life-saving equipment
is too expensive.

47:54.746 --> 47:57.082
It doesn't make sense
if you know the cost of it.

47:57.165 --> 47:59.293
And lots of other countries
have figured it out.

47:59.376 --> 48:00.419
Say one that does.

48:00.502 --> 48:01.920
The UK, USA,

48:02.004 --> 48:03.422
- Australia, and Japan.
- The UK?

48:04.298 --> 48:06.967
You know the UK's annual budget
for the Meteorological Administration?

48:07.050 --> 48:09.011
1.6 trillion won.

48:09.094 --> 48:10.721
That's four times what we have.

48:10.804 --> 48:12.222
The US? Japan?

48:12.306 --> 48:13.557
- Australia?
- Whatever.

48:13.640 --> 48:15.517
This is why you research
before publishing!

48:16.018 --> 48:18.186
Do your research
and make sure you understand!

48:18.270 --> 48:19.229
And if you can't…

48:21.064 --> 48:23.609
there are people you know
that can check your work.

48:29.698 --> 48:32.451
You didn't intentionally overlook this,
or did you?

48:33.285 --> 48:36.538
Are you acting out of spite?
Letting things slide, so you can hurt me?

48:48.675 --> 48:49.593
It was unintentional.

48:50.886 --> 48:52.721
I'll take care of it from here.

48:52.804 --> 48:54.306
You can go back to your work.

48:58.936 --> 49:00.145
It's your job

49:01.855 --> 49:03.398
to deal with the press.

49:04.149 --> 49:05.359
Deal with it.

49:11.323 --> 49:12.532
You're angry?

49:12.616 --> 49:14.785
Let's find some privacy. We'll talk there.

49:16.411 --> 49:17.663
What are you gonna take care of?

49:18.288 --> 49:19.790
This mess of an article,

49:19.873 --> 49:22.501
I have to take care of it,
'cause that's what I do here.

49:26.129 --> 49:28.090
You have to be ready
if you do stuff like that.

49:28.173 --> 49:30.467
Ha-kyung's smart. There's a reason

49:30.550 --> 49:32.761
she's the youngest director
the division's ever had.

49:32.844 --> 49:34.137
So what now?

49:34.221 --> 49:36.556
You used to confuse probability
of detection with accuracy

49:36.640 --> 49:39.309
when you first started coming here,
but now you're just picking fight.

49:39.393 --> 49:40.852
Why are you bringing that up again?

49:40.936 --> 49:42.312
Come on, you know better than that.

49:42.396 --> 49:43.814
You should've notified me
before submitting.

49:43.897 --> 49:46.483
I tried, I asked you to get me
an interview yesterday.

49:46.566 --> 49:50.112
And I told you to wait! Then I could have
proofread it to double-check!

49:50.696 --> 49:51.530
Double-check?

49:52.114 --> 49:54.449
Reporters don't ask their subjects
to check their work.

49:54.533 --> 49:56.243
It's rude. I'm a journalist.

49:56.326 --> 49:59.246
It's my job to keep an eye on you
and keep you in check.

50:01.915 --> 50:03.125
That's ridiculous.

50:03.208 --> 50:05.002
'Cause you're not logical or factual.

50:05.085 --> 50:06.795
A real journalist
never would have published that.

50:06.878 --> 50:08.714
- That's mean.
- You wouldn't have to lie

50:08.797 --> 50:11.008
- if you were such a great reporter.
- I didn't lie.

50:11.091 --> 50:13.593
- It was the truth, she said everything.
- Lee Si-woo.

50:15.721 --> 50:17.055
You've never met him?

50:26.440 --> 50:27.816
Another fact?

50:40.579 --> 50:41.872
Oh…

50:48.462 --> 50:50.505
Oh, I think she's getting yelled at. Huh?

50:51.173 --> 50:53.800
Probably. She should've known
not to do an interview.

50:54.676 --> 50:57.679
She would've lost
even if she had declined.

50:57.763 --> 51:01.099
'Cause people would think
she's still hung up on him, you know?

51:02.726 --> 51:06.480
Goes to show, breaking up
with a co-worker is even more painful.

51:06.980 --> 51:09.524
Not that marrying one
is anything to brag about.

51:09.608 --> 51:11.777
Just don't date in the workplace.

51:11.860 --> 51:12.861
Hm.

51:23.038 --> 51:24.081
I apologize.

51:24.164 --> 51:26.500
She said she needed help with her article.

51:26.583 --> 51:29.336
I should've chosen my words
much more carefully.

51:29.419 --> 51:30.629
That's true.

51:32.923 --> 51:35.550
What else?
I assume that you called her out.

51:37.135 --> 51:38.970
Yes. I was just so angry.

51:40.097 --> 51:41.014
Well done.

51:43.100 --> 51:46.853
The reporters just want a hit piece
and we're an easy target.

51:46.937 --> 51:47.979
You should get angry.

51:48.730 --> 51:51.775
We take criticism in stride,
but if you think about it,

51:52.359 --> 51:54.778
if these reporters
are not held accountable by us,

51:54.861 --> 51:56.196
who's going to do it?

51:56.279 --> 51:57.656
You did well.

51:58.281 --> 52:00.325
Ah. I have a job for you.

52:01.076 --> 52:02.869
You're gonna write a response article.

52:03.912 --> 52:07.958
Hm? Using logic and facts,
and you'll explain the real reason

52:08.041 --> 52:10.210
we don't do fog advisories in Korea.

52:10.794 --> 52:13.004
I can't let you write that
if it's a direct response.

52:13.880 --> 52:15.090
Get pretty close, though.

52:15.674 --> 52:17.884
- Okay?
- Yes, I'll get started.

52:37.445 --> 52:38.864
How can I help you?

52:43.702 --> 52:47.122
I overheard that they're having you
draft a new article

52:47.873 --> 52:49.207
to clarify your stands on fog.

52:50.417 --> 52:51.626
Yes. And?

52:52.210 --> 52:54.296
I wanted to know your timeline.

52:55.005 --> 52:57.549
It's not set.
I've quite a bit of data to review.

52:58.133 --> 53:01.469
Well, I'd really appreciate your draft
as soon as possible.

53:02.262 --> 53:03.388
I need it

53:04.598 --> 53:06.433
to write the official rebuttal.

53:10.187 --> 53:11.730
You really didn't know?

53:19.863 --> 53:22.449
No, I didn't.

53:25.660 --> 53:27.078
I thought that after marriage,

53:27.162 --> 53:30.248
a couple starts to communicate even more,
be more open.

53:31.249 --> 53:32.876
I've been wrong before.

53:35.503 --> 53:37.589
I can get the draft to you
tomorrow morning.

53:37.672 --> 53:38.590
All right?

53:57.859 --> 53:59.444
What? You what?

54:00.612 --> 54:03.114
She met with a matchmaker,
did the ranking quiz,

54:03.198 --> 54:04.241
and decided to sign you up.

54:06.284 --> 54:07.994
I think it'll be good for you.

54:08.078 --> 54:10.538
Since you've been acting
like such a lovesick baby,

54:11.414 --> 54:14.876
I couldn't sit by any longer.
I know what you're worth.

54:14.960 --> 54:17.754
If you're not going to find
yourself a husband, I will.

54:19.089 --> 54:20.674
Oh, good job. She took it real well.

54:22.509 --> 54:24.886
I did it, 'cause I love you so very much!

54:24.970 --> 54:29.015
Huh? And then you could go and marry
a kind man who is successful.

54:29.099 --> 54:31.476
And everyone at your work
would be impressed, too.

54:31.559 --> 54:34.020
So just forget about Ki-jun already,
that bastard.

54:34.104 --> 54:35.689
I know you know I'm right.

54:36.273 --> 54:37.941
You've got a lot of confidence, Ma.

54:38.566 --> 54:41.278
Can't you be on my side once? Traitor.

54:52.163 --> 54:54.541
Ha-kyung, what are you doing?

54:54.624 --> 54:57.252
- I think she's gonna leave, Ma.
- What?

54:57.335 --> 54:58.670
You… You're not going, are you?

54:59.713 --> 55:02.757
Go back to the matchmaker
and have her delete the profile.

55:02.841 --> 55:04.342
Shut it down.

55:04.426 --> 55:05.927
You can call me when it's done.

55:06.636 --> 55:09.597
You can't, you know how expensive it was.

55:11.099 --> 55:12.892
- Ha-kyung.
- Wait!

55:12.976 --> 55:15.228
- I knew it! You wouldn't listen!
- I need shoes. Ha-kyung!

56:41.314 --> 56:44.275
UNTITLED5.MP3
SEARCH FILES

56:57.288 --> 56:59.457
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

57:03.628 --> 57:06.047
Hello, Director Jin.
Is everything all right?

57:06.131 --> 57:08.508
- Were you asleep?
- No, I wasn't.

57:08.591 --> 57:10.009
Oh, good.

57:10.093 --> 57:15.223
I looked over your report on the UK,
and I'm confused by the translations.

57:15.306 --> 57:16.307
Can you help?

57:26.234 --> 57:27.277
Uh, where is it?

57:27.360 --> 57:29.112
It's on page 12.

57:29.195 --> 57:31.197
In the second chapter.

57:31.281 --> 57:32.907
Okay. One minute.

57:34.117 --> 57:35.243
Okay.

57:36.578 --> 57:37.871
Hm…

57:45.962 --> 57:47.380
INCOMING CALL
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

57:49.883 --> 57:50.800
Yeah?

57:51.468 --> 57:53.761
Page 27, Table 3-1.

57:53.845 --> 57:55.597
Was there a graph, too?

58:08.943 --> 58:10.195
Yeah?

58:10.278 --> 58:13.364
Is there any reason I can't use
the Sydney case for reference?

58:13.448 --> 58:14.657
It has so many singularities.

58:16.618 --> 58:17.869
Uh…

58:18.745 --> 58:20.163
Are you still there?

58:20.788 --> 58:23.458
Yeah, I'm here. One minute.

59:04.207 --> 59:05.250
What are you doing here?

59:05.333 --> 59:07.710
It's easier than having you call
every five seconds.

59:07.794 --> 59:09.546
Well, I haven't called in 30 minutes, so…

59:09.629 --> 59:11.256
Staying up made me hungry,

59:11.339 --> 59:13.550
so I had to go out, anyway,
to get some food.

59:13.633 --> 59:15.260
And I thought you might want some, too.

59:19.889 --> 59:21.182
Okay.

59:24.686 --> 59:25.770
Here.

59:29.649 --> 59:31.609
Oh, there are toppings on it.

59:32.527 --> 59:33.444
Yeah, so?

59:34.028 --> 59:36.823
I don't get toppings on pizza.

59:38.032 --> 59:40.034
I can fix that. Here.

59:41.035 --> 59:42.745
Flip one over.

59:43.997 --> 59:45.707
It's not pizza, it's a sandwich.

59:47.584 --> 59:49.002
Mmm!

59:49.711 --> 59:50.712
Is it good?

59:52.589 --> 59:53.590
Have some.

59:55.049 --> 59:56.426
- Flip it?
- Yeah.

59:56.509 --> 59:59.345
- Put them together?
- Just like the sandwich. Yeah.

59:59.429 --> 01:00:01.347
You'll like it.

01:00:01.431 --> 01:00:02.599
- Cheers.
- Yeah.

01:00:04.475 --> 01:00:05.560
It's good, right?

01:00:06.436 --> 01:00:09.647
Dig in, please.

01:00:23.036 --> 01:00:25.496
Yeah, this one was from the UK.

01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:28.374
There should be
the original copy of the article.

01:00:28.458 --> 01:00:29.876
- Can you find it?
- Oh, yeah.

01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:31.919
Here it is.

01:00:32.003 --> 01:00:34.422
I marked all of the most important parts
in blue for you.

01:00:34.505 --> 01:00:35.673
See there?

01:00:37.342 --> 01:00:39.385
I think it needs to be simpler.

01:00:39.469 --> 01:00:42.221
- Hm?
- You should break it down.

01:00:42.305 --> 01:00:43.848
What do you think?

01:00:47.143 --> 01:00:48.853
I think it's good for a draft.

01:00:49.437 --> 01:00:50.563
You think?

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:11.876
How do you feel, though,
about me?

01:01:14.087 --> 01:01:15.630
I shouldn't have revealed it.

01:01:16.381 --> 01:01:17.590
Sorry.

01:01:22.136 --> 01:01:23.471
I'm not sorry at all.

01:01:25.264 --> 01:01:28.893
Why would I be sorry that you
could see I wanna be with you?

01:01:32.522 --> 01:01:33.940
I really do.

01:03:00.151 --> 01:03:02.111
Oh? Why are you here so late?

01:03:02.195 --> 01:03:04.530
Oh, it's been so busy.

01:03:05.114 --> 01:03:08.034
I missed my shot. Si-woo has a girlfriend.

01:03:10.578 --> 01:03:11.746
Where did you hear that?

01:03:12.914 --> 01:03:15.082
Everybody's been talking about her.

01:03:15.666 --> 01:03:18.002
He said that she works here at KMA.

01:03:30.348 --> 01:03:31.974
Isn't it beautiful?

01:03:33.476 --> 01:03:34.727
It is.

01:03:35.728 --> 01:03:37.814
Sunrise is my favorite part of the day.

01:03:38.439 --> 01:03:40.358
I didn't know you're a morning person.

01:03:42.819 --> 01:03:44.028
Tell me more.

01:03:50.326 --> 01:03:53.454
I don't wanna sell this place yet.

01:03:56.916 --> 01:03:58.417
It makes me think of what happened.

01:03:59.001 --> 01:04:01.671
I need some new memories here,
so the old ones will fade.

01:04:05.842 --> 01:04:07.093
Tell me more.

01:04:07.677 --> 01:04:10.096
Well, what do you wanna know about me?

01:04:10.721 --> 01:04:11.889
Everything.

01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:16.602
I wanna know everything. If that's okay.

01:04:17.270 --> 01:04:18.521
Everything.

01:04:21.983 --> 01:04:23.401
Didn't I ask for discretion?

01:04:24.151 --> 01:04:25.987
Well, we're not at the office, so…

01:04:28.155 --> 01:04:32.326
You know we have to end this
if they ever found out, you know?

01:04:34.036 --> 01:04:35.162
I know.

01:04:36.622 --> 01:04:40.585
And I'd have to put up walls to keep them
from getting suspicious of us.

01:04:42.128 --> 01:04:43.296
I know.

01:04:44.213 --> 01:04:45.506
I can take it.

01:04:48.759 --> 01:04:51.429
Visibility is the maximum distance

01:04:51.512 --> 01:04:52.930
that can be seen with the naked eye.

01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:54.891
You have a girlfriend?

01:05:02.607 --> 01:05:04.317
No. Not right now.

01:05:05.067 --> 01:05:07.612
- You'll have it soon?
- Yeah, of course. Right away.

01:05:07.695 --> 01:05:10.031
What? She's messing with him, right?

01:05:10.114 --> 01:05:12.533
She must be.
Maybe he did something.

01:05:22.585 --> 01:05:24.503
Depending on the surrounding conditions,

01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:28.049
the naked eyesight
may be heavily distorted.

01:05:29.425 --> 01:05:33.804
I'd appreciate if you'd avoid small talk
during working hours, Forecaster Lee.

01:05:34.472 --> 01:05:36.057
Thanks for this. You may go.

01:05:36.974 --> 01:05:38.601
It can be narrowed.

01:05:39.727 --> 01:05:41.687
Yes, can I help you?

01:05:41.771 --> 01:05:43.731
Uh, no. I'm all good.

01:05:46.901 --> 01:05:48.861
And it can be distorted.

01:05:50.404 --> 01:05:53.199
I don't ever want people
to know that I'm dating a colleague.

01:05:53.282 --> 01:05:54.533
I know that.

01:05:55.534 --> 01:05:57.161
What if we break down each area?

01:05:57.244 --> 01:06:00.957
And we can emphasize the valleys,
streams, and any other unique areas.

01:06:11.258 --> 01:06:13.135
It seems like right now,

01:06:13.219 --> 01:06:16.681
our visibility is low,
so we'll have to be careful.

01:06:18.349 --> 01:06:21.560
What happens if someone catches us?

01:06:22.603 --> 01:06:25.189
We'd fuss up and end things.

01:06:26.565 --> 01:06:27.566
Oh.

01:06:28.234 --> 01:06:29.360
That's exciting.

01:06:30.653 --> 01:06:33.531
I can't go through all that.
I've learned my lesson.

01:06:34.156 --> 01:06:35.366
Okay?

01:07:04.103 --> 01:07:07.898
We all ran into bad weather,
dense fog,

01:07:07.982 --> 01:07:11.277
yellow dust, unexpected rain, or snow.

01:07:46.771 --> 01:07:49.523
But bad weather
teaches us something.

01:07:54.987 --> 01:07:58.407
It teaches us
that the best way to improve visibility

01:07:58.491 --> 01:08:03.996
is to be brave and move closer
to reduce your distance from the target.

01:08:25.601 --> 01:08:26.519
I'm late.

01:08:46.455 --> 01:08:47.748
I'm not ready yet.

01:08:47.832 --> 01:08:50.251
- Oh, no, we can't go in together.
- We're gonna be late, though.

01:08:50.334 --> 01:08:51.836
Not we, just you.

01:08:59.260 --> 01:09:00.469
EFFECTIVENESS OF FOG ADVISORIES
AND CASES FROM ABROAD

01:09:23.868 --> 01:09:25.035
Hello?

01:09:53.397 --> 01:09:56.025
How did you cross paths
with Director Jin this morning?

01:09:56.108 --> 01:09:57.526
- We met on our way here.
- Pardon?

01:09:57.610 --> 01:09:58.444
It was a coincidence.

01:09:58.527 --> 01:10:01.405
Who said you could
keep crossing lines like that?

01:10:01.488 --> 01:10:03.908
Did you want to see
how I would react if I saw you with him?

01:10:03.991 --> 01:10:06.076
Call me outside like this
one more time…

01:10:06.160 --> 01:10:07.244
Forecaster Lee, you…

01:10:07.328 --> 01:10:09.205
Do you know of a heart
that asks for permission to beat?

01:10:09.288 --> 01:10:11.999
Get it together, Forecaster Lee!

01:10:12.082 --> 01:10:13.751
It's the Metropolitan Office.

01:10:13.834 --> 01:10:15.961
They're saying the rain echo
over Seoul looks abnormal.

01:10:16.045 --> 01:10:17.338
Could you take a look?
